# Zod Organization

Use `zod/mini`. Keep each Zod schema and its inferred TypeScript types in the
**same file**. Do **not** peel `z.infer<>` types into a separate `*.types.ts`.

Within a Zod-bearing file, use clear section markers:

1. imports / file header
2. constants / helpers needed by schemas (if any)
3. `[schemas]` — all Zod schemas together
4. `[types]` — all `z.infer<>` and related exported types together
5. parse helpers / other functions (optional)

`*.types.ts` remains for **non-Zod** implementation/API types (for example
producer ClickHouseWriter options). See [type-organization.mdc](./type-organization.mdc).

```typescript
// BAD: Zod-inferred type extracted to filters.types.ts
// filters.ts
export const FindingFiltersSchema = z.partialRecord(/* ... */);
// filters.types.ts
export type FindingFilters = z.infer<typeof FindingFiltersSchema>;

// GOOD: same file, sectioned
// [schemas]
export const FindingFiltersSchema = z.partialRecord(/* ... */);

// [types]
export type FindingFilters = z.infer<typeof FindingFiltersSchema>;
```
